To 'greeting for' of a number called id.
    Return a text, "hi {id}".

To 'framed' of a text called word.
    a buffer called frame is "[".
    append word to frame.
    append "]" to frame.
    Return a buffer, frame.

Open a file for writing called notes at "./call_write_source.txt".
Write 'greeting for' of 1 to notes.
Write a newline to notes.
Write {'greeting for' of 2} to notes.
Write a newline to notes.
Write 'framed' of "x" to notes.
Write a newline to notes.
Close notes.
Open a file for reading called written at "./call_write_source.txt".
a buffer called contents is 1024 bytes in size.
Read from written into contents.
Close written.
Delete "./call_write_source.txt".
Print contents without newline.
a buffer called sink is "".
append {'greeting for' of 3} to sink.
append 'greeting for' of 4 to sink.
append 'framed' of "y" to sink.
append {'framed' of "z"} to sink.
Print sink.
